# Ownership for the paths that decide what gets signed, what gets shipped, and
# what the app is allowed to do.
#
# The point is not bureaucracy. `main` is protected and the release workflow
# holds the Apple Developer ID certificate and the notarisation credentials, so
# a change to the workflow, to a release script, or to the entitlements is a
# change to the trust story of every published build — and those are exactly the
# files that look boring in a diff.
#
# With a single maintainer this file documents intent and does nothing to
# enforce it. Once there is a second, add them below and turn on "Require review
# from Code Owners" in the ruleset for `main`, which is the point at which it
# starts being a control rather than a note.

